## Web Frontend Route Protection (`packages/web`)

The root route (`packages/web/src/routes/__root.tsx`, line 15–20) fetches the session once at the top of every navigation:
```ts
beforeLoad: async () => {
  const { data: session } = await authClient.getSession();
  return { user: session?.user as User | undefined };
},
```
This puts `context.user` into the router context for all child routes.

### Protected layout: `/_app` (`packages/web/src/routes/_app.tsx`)
Any route nested under `/_app` is protected — its `beforeLoad` checks `context.user` and redirects to `/login` if absent:
```ts
beforeLoad: ({ context, location }) => {
  if (!context.user) {
    throw redirect({ to: "/login", search: { redirect: location.href } });
  }
},
```
**A route opts in to auth protection by being a child of `/_app`** in the file-based route tree. Public pages (login, etc.) sit under `/_authentication` instead, which does the inverse check.

